          {
            "id": 27,
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "align": "start",
            "text": "Orders are packed on the day they are placed and leave the warehouse by the first van of the morning. Pens are sold in boxes of twelve and paper by the ream, tape and glue by the single roll or the single tube. A box that arrives damaged is replaced without charge if the carrier is told within three working days. Prices include delivery to any address in the country and are held until the end of the quarter. Stock levels are counted on the first of the month and the figures above are those of the last count. Questions about a figure go to the purchasing office and questions about a delivery go to the warehouse. The office is open from eight until five on weekdays and from nine until noon on the first Saturday. A recorded message gives the numbers to ring at night and on the days when the office is closed. Nothing in this note changes the terms of an order that has been agreed in writing before today.",
